To specify the API key when creating a new Anthropic client in the Python and TypeScript SDK examples, you can do the following:

Python:
```python
import os
from anthropic import Client

# Option 1: Set the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY environment variable
os.environ["ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"] = "your-api-key-here"
client = Client()

# Option 2: Pass the API key directly to the Client constructor
client = Client(api_key="your-api-key-here")
```

TypeScript:
```typescript
import { Configuration, OpenAIApi } from "openai";

// Option 1: Set the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY environment variable
process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = "your-api-key-here";
const client = new OpenAIApi(new Configuration());

// Option 2: Pass the API key directly to the Configuration constructor
const configuration = new Configuration({
  apiKey: "your-api-key-here",
});
const client = new OpenAIApi(configuration);
```

